WEBVTT

00:04.070 --> 00:08.030
Wow, love that blazer!

00:08.860 --> 00:11.030
You'd look right at home on a TV show.

00:11.030 --> 00:11.840
Yeah?

00:11.840 --> 00:12.700
Yup.

00:12.700 --> 00:14.790
It looks great on ya.

00:14.790 --> 00:17.160
You're our pride and joy, Mitsumi-chan.

00:17.550 --> 00:18.800
Pride and joy...

00:18.800 --> 00:20.810
Anyway, I gotta run.

00:20.810 --> 00:23.660
Can't be late for the entrance
ceremony, ya know?

00:23.660 --> 00:25.290
Later!

00:25.290 --> 00:26.880
Yeah, bye.

00:28.740 --> 00:31.260
I'm Iwakura Mitsumi, fifteen years old.

00:35.060 --> 00:38.440
And my life as a Tokyo
high schooler starts today!

02:15.490 --> 02:19.170
I came here from a tiny, remote town
on the border of Ishikawa Prefecture.

02:19.170 --> 02:22.170
Mitsumi-chan!

02:24.070 --> 02:27.660
I'll be back for summer break!

02:28.660 --> 02:30.310
Take care!
Break a leg!

02:30.310 --> 02:31.470
Take care!

02:32.010 --> 02:34.860
I wish I coulda sent you off like that.

02:34.860 --> 02:37.000
Haha, I know that feeling.

02:37.000 --> 02:41.140
The nearest train line got shut down
more than a decade ago.

02:41.140 --> 02:43.750
My middle school only had
eight students in my year.

02:43.750 --> 02:46.020
Here, Mitsumi-chan.

02:46.020 --> 02:48.680
Fumi-chan and I have been
together since kindergarten.

02:48.680 --> 02:49.940
Cute.

02:49.940 --> 02:51.310
I know you like pandas.

02:51.780 --> 02:54.730
If you see Liang Liang, send me pics.

02:54.730 --> 02:56.180
She's my best friend.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.190
You got it.

02:59.000 --> 03:01.960
Growing up with my best friend.
How cool is that?

03:49.770 --> 03:53.310
Heh. Perfect.

03:53.310 --> 03:55.070
Listen, Mitsu.

03:55.070 --> 03:57.490
Change trains at the third stop, 'kay?

03:57.490 --> 03:59.800
This is Nao-chan, my dad's sibling.

03:59.800 --> 04:02.770
If anyone strange talks to you,
just ignore them.

04:02.770 --> 04:04.730
She's taking care of me while I'm in Tokyo.

04:04.730 --> 04:06.660
You worry too much, Nao-chan.

04:06.660 --> 04:07.830
Can you blame me?

04:07.830 --> 04:11.560
You only just found out that there's
more than one railway company!

04:11.560 --> 04:14.430
I wish I could go with you,
but my work starts early today!

04:14.430 --> 04:15.310
Relax.

04:15.310 --> 04:19.950
My intuition tells me that today
will be nothing short of perfect.

04:23.450 --> 04:24.450
Plenty of time.

04:25.070 --> 04:26.720
It won't just be today.

04:26.720 --> 04:31.050
There will be zero screwups for the
entirety of my time in high school.

04:31.050 --> 04:35.330
Why? Because I have
a clear road map for my life!

04:36.520 --> 04:38.500
I will obviously go to Tokyo U,

04:38.500 --> 04:40.720
attend law school,
and graduate as valedictorian.

04:40.720 --> 04:42.160
I'll join the Ministry of Internal Affairs

04:42.160 --> 04:45.580
and build a career there providing
key solutions to rural depopulation.

04:45.580 --> 04:48.420
After I retire, I'll return to my
hometown and become mayor there,

04:48.420 --> 04:52.890
using the knowledge from my career
to greatly improve our finances.

04:52.890 --> 04:55.960
And when I die, I'll have my ashes
scattered in the Sea of Japan.

04:56.890 --> 05:02.490
In the next three years, I'll develop
the brains I need to fulfill those ambitions!

05:03.080 --> 05:06.650
However, my family doesn't
really get it, which is why...

05:06.650 --> 05:08.260
Are you having fun at school?

05:08.260 --> 05:09.940
Made any friends?

05:09.940 --> 05:12.090
They'll probably worry about those things,

05:12.090 --> 05:14.960
so I'll try to put them at ease, too.

05:17.590 --> 05:19.240
Just wait and see, you guys.

05:19.960 --> 05:22.090
Ikajima Town's prodigy, your pride and joy,

05:22.090 --> 05:24.570
will return to you as a total big shot!

05:25.390 --> 05:27.010
Third stop, third stop...

05:30.740 --> 05:34.600
The entrance ceremony for Tsubame
West High School will now begin.

05:35.490 --> 05:37.450
Please welcome the new first-years.

05:38.450 --> 05:40.230
Hey, Sousuke?

05:40.230 --> 05:41.590
Where are you?

05:41.590 --> 05:43.730
Changing trains now.

05:43.730 --> 05:45.300
Taking it easy, huh?

05:45.300 --> 05:46.970
The entrance ceremony's already started.

05:46.970 --> 05:48.240
Oh, really?

05:48.240 --> 05:50.140
Maybe I should just go home, then.

05:50.140 --> 05:51.730
At least try to get here, dude.

05:51.730 --> 05:52.410
But...

05:52.410 --> 05:54.080
I probably won't make...

06:01.110 --> 06:02.420
She's stuck.

06:02.420 --> 06:03.130
Wha?

06:03.620 --> 06:05.760
A girl in our uniform.
She's stuck to the wall.

06:06.370 --> 06:07.650
She crazy, you think?

06:07.650 --> 06:09.760
Beats me. Why don't you ask her?

06:09.760 --> 06:11.850
I gotta go, so I'm hanging up.

06:12.420 --> 06:13.870
Are you a first-year?

06:13.870 --> 06:14.560
Yes.

06:14.560 --> 06:16.880
The others have already entered.

06:16.880 --> 06:18.720
Sorry. I was fighting for my life in there.

06:18.720 --> 06:19.720
Get going!

06:19.720 --> 06:20.480
Yes, sir.

06:20.480 --> 06:22.340
You still can't reach her?

06:22.340 --> 06:23.480
No...

06:23.480 --> 06:26.100
What do we do?

06:26.100 --> 06:28.360
What's going on with Class 3?

06:37.370 --> 06:37.940
Huh? Where am I?
Do I go that way? This way?

06:37.940 --> 06:39.240
I got lost...
Huh? Where am I?
Do I go that way? This way?

06:39.240 --> 06:40.040
Huh? Where am I?
Do I go that way? This way?

06:40.040 --> 06:42.290
Got caught in rush hour...

06:42.730 --> 06:44.030
And got sick from the crowd.

06:46.650 --> 06:48.790
This wasn't the plan.

06:49.240 --> 06:50.640
I wanna die.

06:51.820 --> 06:53.100
Hey...

06:53.690 --> 06:55.660
Are you okay?

06:59.620 --> 07:00.830
Yikes!

07:01.400 --> 07:03.310
Actually, never mind.

07:04.730 --> 07:05.980
Eek!

07:05.980 --> 07:07.200
H...

07:07.200 --> 07:08.490
H-Huh?

07:11.620 --> 07:17.190
How many years has it been
since I spoke to a stranger my age?

07:17.190 --> 07:17.870
How...

07:17.870 --> 07:21.120
How do I get to school from here?!

07:29.930 --> 07:31.720
Oh, you're lost?

07:32.130 --> 07:33.520
I'm running late, too.

07:34.100 --> 07:35.600
Let's go together.

07:37.390 --> 07:41.010
High school, college, and employment...

07:41.010 --> 07:44.390
They're, uh... all about
the people you meet.

07:44.390 --> 07:45.150
Er...

07:45.150 --> 07:49.650
After passing our rigorous
entrance exams, uhm...

07:50.120 --> 07:52.880
Oh, really? You're from Ishikawa?

07:52.880 --> 07:53.920
Yes...

07:53.920 --> 07:54.950
Which city?

07:54.950 --> 07:55.670
Yes...

07:55.670 --> 07:57.900
I've never been to Ishikawa.

07:57.900 --> 07:59.810
What if I don't make it in time?

07:59.810 --> 08:02.430
I know I'm gonna get
a call from home today.

08:02.430 --> 08:04.540
They'll ask how the entrance ceremony went.

08:04.540 --> 08:07.500
If I tell the truth, they'll worry about me.

08:08.200 --> 08:09.760
Should I lie?

08:09.760 --> 08:11.440
About all of it?

08:12.790 --> 08:15.340
Hey, it's not the end of the world.

08:15.340 --> 08:17.300
It's just the entrance ceremony.

08:21.560 --> 08:23.810
Maybe that's all it is to you!

08:26.360 --> 08:27.310
W-Wait, no!

08:27.310 --> 08:27.860
We will soon be making
a brief stop at Miyamaeyama.

08:27.860 --> 08:30.190
Oh, here's our stop.
We will soon be making
a brief stop at Miyamaeyama.

08:30.190 --> 08:32.380
The doors on the right side will open.

08:35.290 --> 08:37.740
It's about a ten-minute walk from here.

08:38.070 --> 08:39.620
But you're in a rush, right?

08:40.060 --> 08:41.110
Wanna run?

08:42.290 --> 08:44.260
Dad. Mom.

08:44.260 --> 08:46.120
Maharu. Kippei.

08:46.120 --> 08:48.770
Granny. Satonosuke.

08:48.770 --> 08:51.260
Omiso. Oshio.

08:51.260 --> 08:53.790
Everything in Tokyo moves at lightning speed.

08:53.790 --> 08:59.440
I got swallowed by its waves.
I panicked, made things worse,

08:59.440 --> 09:00.640
and in the end...

09:03.370 --> 09:05.520
It's straight down this road. Hang in there.

09:06.440 --> 09:10.160
I lashed out at this kind, helpful guy.

09:11.850 --> 09:15.200
I feel like I've seen my own
true colors in just half a day.

09:16.520 --> 09:17.660
I'm ashamed of myself.

09:20.310 --> 09:22.500
Y-You okay?

09:25.260 --> 09:27.250
I'm... fine...

09:28.260 --> 09:31.690
But for now, I'm gonna forget all that...

09:32.580 --> 09:34.070
and run for my life!

10:47.930 --> 10:48.540
Oh!

10:48.540 --> 10:50.070
Iwakura-san?!

10:50.070 --> 10:51.250
...es...

10:51.250 --> 10:52.810
Shima-kun?

10:52.810 --> 10:55.130
Yes. Sorry we're late.

10:55.130 --> 10:56.520
Sor...

10:56.520 --> 10:59.050
There, there. I'm glad you made it.

10:59.050 --> 11:01.130
Wait, are you okay, Iwakura-san?

11:01.550 --> 11:02.770
Did I... make...

11:02.770 --> 11:03.640
Yikes!

11:03.640 --> 11:05.720
Yes, you're just in time.

11:05.720 --> 11:08.850
Be sure to thank the person
we asked to sub in for you.

11:08.850 --> 11:10.330
I will. I'm sorry.

11:10.330 --> 11:11.480
Hmm?

11:12.000 --> 11:15.100
Representing the incoming class,
Iwakura Mitsumi.

11:15.100 --> 11:16.070
Yes!

11:21.500 --> 11:23.390
You're top of the class?

11:29.690 --> 11:30.460
Urk.

11:31.450 --> 11:32.320
"Urk"?

11:34.750 --> 11:36.620
Wait, did she forget her script?!

11:47.890 --> 11:50.410
As the warmth of spring rolls in,

11:50.410 --> 11:56.480
we 216 students stand here at the entrance
ceremony for Tsubame West High School.

11:56.860 --> 12:00.990
On behalf of my class, I would like to
thank you all for this wonderful ceremony.

12:00.990 --> 12:02.620
She memorized it?
On behalf of my class, I would like to
thank you all for this wonderful ceremony.

12:02.620 --> 12:03.570
Whoa.

12:03.570 --> 12:08.060
Our hearts are filled with hopes and fears,

12:08.060 --> 12:12.420
just like the sakura trees in the school
courtyard, with flowers yet to blossom.

12:12.420 --> 12:14.810
The experience of overcoming
the tough entrance exams

12:14.810 --> 12:18.930
will give us confidence and strength
to overcome the days ahead.

12:18.930 --> 12:20.040
Haha...

12:20.710 --> 12:24.810
None of us could have made it this far alone.

12:24.810 --> 12:29.300
We must remember the support we
received from our families and friends,

12:29.300 --> 12:31.290
try to live up to their expectations,

12:31.290 --> 12:35.290
and in our time at Tsubame West,
think for ourselves...

12:36.070 --> 12:43.400
I'm blessed to join a school that values
independence, individuality, and autonomy.

12:43.800 --> 12:45.480
And, last but not least,

12:45.480 --> 12:48.660
to the teachers and the older students:

12:48.660 --> 12:52.900
We hope that you will watch over
and guide us new students.

12:52.900 --> 12:55.020
Thank you.

12:55.020 --> 12:57.480
She didn't blink once!

13:14.610 --> 13:16.270
Iwakura-san? Where are you go—

13:16.270 --> 13:17.310
Huh?

13:29.530 --> 13:31.190
The script for today:

13:32.120 --> 13:33.150
One.

13:35.120 --> 13:35.730
Two.

13:35.730 --> 13:38.330
That was a great speech!

13:38.330 --> 13:39.110
Three.

13:39.110 --> 13:41.460
Let's be friends!

13:42.090 --> 13:43.770
Oh, the puker?

13:43.770 --> 13:44.890
This is concerning.

13:44.890 --> 13:46.340
The puker, huh?

13:46.340 --> 13:49.740
Day one, and I'm the puker.

13:49.740 --> 13:53.460
But wait, I can salvage that if I try.

13:53.460 --> 13:55.900
Oh, I listen to them, too!

13:55.900 --> 13:57.590
Aren't they great?

13:57.590 --> 13:59.370
Hey, let's trade contact details.

13:59.370 --> 14:01.770
Really? I'd love to.

14:02.430 --> 14:03.680
Did you get it?

14:04.590 --> 14:07.380
W-Wow. I should learn from them.
Hah, what is this sticker? It's cute!

14:07.380 --> 14:08.240
W-Wow. I should learn from them.

14:08.240 --> 14:09.320
Hey!

14:11.090 --> 14:13.210
I-It's nice to meet you.

14:14.680 --> 14:16.710
Yeah, same here.

14:17.800 --> 14:20.640
I feel like she just brushed me off.

14:20.640 --> 14:21.910
By the way, did you watch their
Pinsta Live a couple of days ago?

14:21.910 --> 14:23.100
Iwakura-san.
By the way, did you watch their
Pinsta Live a couple of days ago?

14:23.100 --> 14:24.850
By the way, did you watch their
Pinsta Live a couple of days ago?

14:24.850 --> 14:26.760
I only realized towards the end.

14:26.760 --> 14:28.170
Guess we're in the same class.

14:28.690 --> 14:29.660
Shima-kun?

14:29.660 --> 14:32.170
That's right. You feeling any better?

14:32.730 --> 14:34.430
Much better now that I hurled.

14:34.430 --> 14:36.560
Oh, good to hear.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.170
I knew it.

14:38.170 --> 14:42.650
I loved your speech. You bossed it up out there.

14:42.650 --> 14:43.370
This guy's a saint!

14:43.370 --> 14:45.200
You weren't even reading notes, were you?
This guy's a saint!

14:45.200 --> 14:45.830
I could never write a speech
like that to save my life.

14:45.830 --> 14:48.510
Oh, I'm suddenly even
finding his face lovely.
I could never write a speech
like that to save my life.

14:48.510 --> 14:49.060
Oh, I'm suddenly even
finding his face lovely.

14:49.060 --> 14:49.420
I really thought you were amazing.
Oh, I'm suddenly even
finding his face lovely.

14:49.420 --> 14:51.360
Is it because he helped me so much today?
I really thought you were amazing.

14:51.360 --> 14:51.950
Is it because he helped me so much today?

14:51.950 --> 14:56.580
Or is Tokyo just filled with
dreamy people like him?

14:57.510 --> 14:59.330
Oh, boy, major stud alert!

14:59.330 --> 15:00.860
He doesn't seem too conceited.

15:00.860 --> 15:02.090
Wonder if he has a girlfriend.

15:02.090 --> 15:03.660
He wasn't in the procession, was he?

15:03.660 --> 15:05.950
I'm so glad I'm in this class.

15:05.950 --> 15:09.080
Iwakura-san, let's be friends.

15:09.080 --> 15:11.340
Oh, give me your ID and stuff.

15:11.340 --> 15:13.480
I'll text you.

15:18.240 --> 15:19.560
Gimme your ID, too.

15:21.060 --> 15:23.620
Oh, I'm Egashira Mika.

15:23.620 --> 15:26.570
I sit right behind you, so I wanna
get to know you better.

15:28.320 --> 15:30.920
I guess my timing was just off earlier.

15:30.920 --> 15:31.790
Sure.

15:32.490 --> 15:35.490
You're Mitsumi-chan? That's a cute name.

15:35.490 --> 15:37.580
Take your seats, everyone.

15:38.040 --> 15:41.920
Sorry I'm late. I had a lot going on.

15:42.620 --> 15:43.830
Forgive me.

15:44.370 --> 15:47.110
I'm Hanazono Sakura,
and I'm in charge of Class 3.

15:47.110 --> 15:52.360
This is my first time as homeroom teacher,
so I'm sure I'll need your help,

15:52.360 --> 15:55.760
but I promise you I'll do my best!
I'm looking forward to working with you all!

15:58.600 --> 16:01.220
Today, I'll give you a simple
intro to your textbooks,

16:01.220 --> 16:04.850
and you'll fill out these profile sheets.
After that, you're free to go.

16:04.850 --> 16:08.180
Tomorrow, you'll introduce
yourselves to the class.

16:08.760 --> 16:10.070
Now, then.

16:10.690 --> 16:12.740
I wonder what my classmates are like.

16:13.990 --> 16:16.540
I'd like to build some solid
relationships with them.

16:18.490 --> 16:20.660
And that's about it, yeah.

16:20.660 --> 16:24.570
No major incidents.
My day was a total success.

16:24.570 --> 16:26.540
Good for ya!

16:26.540 --> 16:31.450
Meanwhile, I was so nervous, I couldn't
respond to people who talked to me.

16:31.450 --> 16:34.300
It's just the first day.
You'll be fine, Fumi.

16:34.300 --> 16:38.300
Ya think? Did ya manage to talk to anyone?

16:38.300 --> 16:41.610
Get this. I made two friends.

16:41.610 --> 16:44.150
Oh, wow! What're they like?

16:44.150 --> 16:46.350
A cute, stylish girl,

16:46.350 --> 16:47.960
and a really nice guy.

16:47.960 --> 16:50.730
Whoa! A guy?!

16:50.730 --> 16:52.070
No way! How?

16:52.070 --> 16:54.800
He helped me this morning when I was los—

16:54.800 --> 16:57.570
er, was close to going the wrong way.

16:57.570 --> 16:59.110
And we wound up in the same class.

16:59.110 --> 17:01.510
Wow... Is he hot?

17:01.510 --> 17:02.280
Ho—

17:03.520 --> 17:06.450
I guess. I've never met
anyone like him before.

17:06.450 --> 17:07.440
Very dapper.

17:07.440 --> 17:09.340
Whoa, lucky you!

17:09.340 --> 17:12.600
But, man, I'd be so lonely
if you got a boyfriend.

17:12.600 --> 17:15.090
Come on, quit jumping the gun!

17:16.210 --> 17:17.930
I better give it my all from tomorrow, too.

17:17.930 --> 17:19.830
Yeah, I'm rooting for you.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.150
I'm home.

17:21.150 --> 17:22.750
Oh, Nao-chan's back.

17:22.750 --> 17:24.040
I'll letcha go, then.

17:24.040 --> 17:28.210
Oh, and take care of my siblings, please?

17:28.210 --> 17:31.110
I'm sure they're gonna miss having me around.

17:31.720 --> 17:32.700
Sure!

17:33.710 --> 17:35.220
Welcome home, Nao-chan.

17:35.220 --> 17:37.120
Sorry I'm late!

17:37.120 --> 17:38.790
How was the entrance ceremony?

17:38.790 --> 17:39.990
It went well.

17:39.990 --> 17:42.200
Really? Thank goodness!

17:42.640 --> 17:44.120
Were you on the phone?

17:44.120 --> 17:45.830
Yeah, was talking to Fumi.

17:45.830 --> 17:47.890
She's feeling helpless
on her own, as expected.

17:47.890 --> 17:52.390
She always has her head in the clouds,
so I worry about her.

17:53.500 --> 17:55.090
Right.

17:55.450 --> 17:57.510
Come, let's eat while we chat.

17:57.510 --> 18:00.180
I bought dinner from
a fancy deli to celebrate.

18:00.180 --> 18:01.640
Thanks!

18:01.640 --> 18:04.790
A deli? Wow, these sides are stylin'.

18:04.790 --> 18:07.030
This place makes the yummiest stuff.

18:07.030 --> 18:10.260
Do kids even say "stylin'" these days?

18:10.260 --> 18:11.360
Yum!

18:11.850 --> 18:14.110
Good evening!

18:14.110 --> 18:16.200
Satonosuke!

18:16.200 --> 18:18.360
Hey there, Fumi-chan.

18:18.360 --> 18:21.140
Brought you some radishes from Mom.

18:21.610 --> 18:24.490
These are so fresh! Thank you!

18:24.490 --> 18:26.570
Oh, do your folks need any asparagus?

18:26.570 --> 18:28.710
I'll fetch some in two
shakes of a lamb's tail.

18:28.710 --> 18:30.410
Fumi-chan, Fumi-chan!

18:30.410 --> 18:31.910
Didya phone Sis?

18:31.910 --> 18:33.040
I just did, yeah.

18:33.040 --> 18:34.130
She say anything?

18:34.130 --> 18:35.580
Like what?

18:35.580 --> 18:38.630
Like, she tells us her day went perfect,

18:38.630 --> 18:43.200
but we were thinking she probably
got lost at the station or something.

18:43.200 --> 18:45.580
I was worried about the same thing.

18:47.140 --> 18:50.950
She's got a screw loose when it comes
to anything 'sides her studies.

18:50.950 --> 18:51.700
Here.

18:51.700 --> 18:54.920
Wow, that's a lot. Thank you.

18:55.520 --> 18:56.900
It'll be fine.

18:56.900 --> 19:00.180
She was happily saying
she made some new pals.

19:00.180 --> 19:02.260
And I'll phone her regularly
to check up on her.

19:02.260 --> 19:03.290
Thank you, dear.

19:03.290 --> 19:06.020
I'll be off, then. Have a good night.

19:09.610 --> 19:12.490
I'd feel a lot better
if Fumi-chan were there with her.

19:12.490 --> 19:13.940
Right?

19:15.210 --> 19:16.980
How was your entrance ceremony?

19:16.980 --> 19:19.000
My class is looking pretty good.

19:19.000 --> 19:19.950
Lucky you.

19:19.950 --> 19:22.840
Mine had this awkward mood from day one.

19:22.840 --> 19:25.110
Hey, don't take my shrimp! I only had four...

19:25.110 --> 19:26.160
Don't be a cheapskate.

19:26.160 --> 19:27.520
Your uniform is real cute.

19:27.520 --> 19:28.840
How about you, Sousuke?

19:28.840 --> 19:29.450
Hmm?

19:29.450 --> 19:32.650
Yeah. How's your little elite school?

19:32.650 --> 19:34.740
I overslept, for one thing.

19:35.270 --> 19:36.530
That was quick!

19:36.530 --> 19:37.590
You didn't make it?

19:37.590 --> 19:39.650
No, I did. I ran from the station.

19:40.420 --> 19:42.110
Who, you?

19:42.590 --> 19:43.610
Yeah.

19:44.170 --> 19:47.620
I thought there wouldn't be a chance in hell,

19:48.600 --> 19:51.220
but the principal's speech
apparently went forever,

19:51.220 --> 19:53.290
so we ended up making it.

19:56.280 --> 19:58.740
That was kinda fun, honestly.

19:59.670 --> 20:00.820
Was it with a girl?

20:00.820 --> 20:03.380
Oh, I should get going.

20:04.660 --> 20:05.570
Lemme out.

20:05.570 --> 20:06.270
Huh?!

20:06.270 --> 20:07.590
Wait, you're leaving already?

20:07.590 --> 20:08.470
Are you serious?

20:08.470 --> 20:10.480
Was it really a girl? That was fast!

20:10.900 --> 20:12.910
Hey, don't run away.

20:12.910 --> 20:15.980
Nah, just thought I'd go home early.

20:16.980 --> 20:19.080
Wouldn't want to be late tomorrow, you know?

20:19.080 --> 20:20.130
Later.

20:25.080 --> 20:26.570
The heck was that?

20:26.570 --> 20:27.410
Don't ask me.

20:28.060 --> 20:31.480
Something must've made him
really happy today.

20:38.680 --> 20:39.560
Yeah.

20:40.730 --> 20:44.090
I might as well enjoy my high school life.

20:49.410 --> 20:51.650
The night lights are so bright here.

20:54.150 --> 20:58.440
Today's mistakes don't count.
It was only my first day, after all.

20:59.690 --> 21:04.090
Also, I did study for the post-entrance exam
and did a bunch of my spring homework.

21:04.090 --> 21:05.070
All good.

21:06.020 --> 21:08.410
I'll be fine from tomorrow.

21:08.410 --> 21:09.780
I know it.

21:17.940 --> 21:20.180
Self-introductions, huh?

21:21.430 --> 21:23.390
Won't be a problem, obviously.

21:26.780 --> 21:29.260
But maybe I should figure out
what I'm gonna say.

21:29.740 --> 21:31.760
First impressions are key.

21:32.440 --> 21:35.140
I'll prepare multiple options
based on the class's mood.

21:53.570 --> 21:55.620
Oh, good morning, Mitsu...

22:02.230 --> 22:04.190
First impressions are...

22:04.190 --> 22:05.240
Yikes!
